    "wire_error_code": false,
    "response_schema_state": "OPEN_OBJECT_OR_HELPER_RETURN",
    "behavioral_preconditions_state": "SELECTED_SOURCE_CALLS_ONLY_NOT_FULLY_ENUMERATED",
    "transitive_error_contract_state": "NOT_ENUMERATED_V1",
    "required_calls_field_semantics": "LEGACY_FIELD_NAME_AST_SYMBOL_PRESENCE_NOT_BRANCH_EXECUTION"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The contract checks source decorators and selected function-level boundaries only.",
    "It does not prove that a server, container, image, network path, database, Bedrock call, or AWS deployment exists.",
    "It does not define exact nested response schemas or every error raised by dependencies and downstream services.",
    "The API currently parses bearer tokens through dependencies but does not declare an OpenAPI security scheme.",
    "Internal agent and llm-gateway routes have no application-layer caller authentication in the AS-IS source.",
    "Company status is recorded but is not enforced as an API authorization gate.",
    "The two-sided data lifecycle section records selected source states; it is not a complete database read/write graph or a policy decision.",
    "A warm recommendation cache can expose an earlier explanation without revalidating the current provider state; the response labels that source but does not resolve the product policy.",
    "Public job detail currently has no open-status filter and can include a closed job plus its company profile.",
    "Authorization-denial audit events retain the actor company and target object reference, not a separate target-company snapshot.",
    "The browser restores its display identity and route role from localStorage without calling the existing auth/me route; protected APIs still resolve the active member DB user from the signed token subject.",
    "The custom bearer token has a fixed synthetic signing-key fallback and no server-side session registry, refresh, logout, or per-token revocation route in the AS-IS source.",
    "Browser session declarations are checked with selected lexical markers, not a JSX control-flow proof or a browser state-transition test."
  ],
